Package: PARROT
Type: Package
Title: Change Point Detection in Dynamic Networks Using SBM
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: person("Chen", "Chen", email = "chenchen9945@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: PARROT (Phase-Altering Regulatory Rewiring Over Time) provides
    efficient algorithms for detecting single and multiple change points in
    dynamic network data. It supports four network types: unipartite weighted,
    unipartite binary, bipartite weighted, and bipartite binary. The package
    uses Stochastic Block Models (SBM) with Variational EM for model fitting,
    Wild Binary Segmentation (WBS) for multiple change point detection, and
    various methods for statistical inference including Wilks' test,
    permutation tests, and parametric bootstrap. C++ acceleration via Rcpp
    provides fast computation for large networks.
